<title>HONG KONG: CKI says signs N.China power projects.</title>
<headline>CKI says signs N.China power projects.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cheung Kong Infrastructure Holdings Ltd said on Wednesday it had signed three contracts to invest 450 million yuan in heat and electricity co-generation plants in northern China of Fushun.</p>
<p>The Hong Kong company also said in a statement it had signed an agreement to invest 200 million yuan in three water plants located in Fushun, Liaoning province.</p>
<p>CKI would have a joint venture period of 20 years in the power plant contracts, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
